# Version-control checkpoints

- After a requested implementation or documentation change is complete and verified, create a focused local Git commit so it can be reverted.
- Before staging, inspect Git status and exclude secrets, private content, generated output and unrelated user changes. Commit only the completed scope.
- A current read-only or no-commit instruction takes precedence. Do not commit incomplete work merely to create a checkpoint.
- Push only when the owner explicitly requests it in the current turn. Never force-push or deploy without separate authorization.
